# Allocator validation (keep passing)

These are not a backlog of unimplemented work. Suites that already exist must **keep passing** when changing the rewrite:

- Compiler-suite **rustc** is compared against **C mimalloc and stock jemalloc**, not only C mimalloc.
- Those rustc (and GCC/Clang) suite cases must **run** under `LD_PRELOAD` and match the system malloc's **stdout, stderr, and exit code**. Compile/link success is not a substitute.
- Keep musl Linux working.

Firefox, Chromium, and Electron are covered by `mimalloc-harness browsers` / `rust/tests/browsers.sh` (libc control must start, spawn children, and finish a short page smoke; rewrite must not regress vs C mimalloc under NixOS `ld-nix.so.preload` injection). Both should pass those smokes: C mimalloc no longer exports `strdup`/`reallocarray`/`__libc_*` by default (`-DMI_OVERRIDE_LIBC_EXTRAS=OFF`) so PartitionAlloc is not handed foreign pointers. Host allocator-exclusion wraps stay required when the OS preloads an older C mimalloc that still exports those aliases.

NixOS-world packages from `/etc/nixos` are covered by `mimalloc-harness world` / `rust/tests/nixos-world.sh`: real workloads (not `--version`) must run under rewrite, C mimalloc, and libc and match stdout/stderr/exit. Explicit coverage includes **python3**, **Node.js**, and **KWin/KDE** (`kwin_wayland --virtual --exit-with-session`, plasmashell, kreadconfig6). Preload both `libmimalloc.so` and `libmimalloc-secure.so.3` so nixpkgs mold's `DT_NEEDED` does not stack C mimalloc. The flake `world-preload` check is the sandboxed subset. The glibc cdylib must DT_NEED `libc.so.6` and must not export unversioned `U atexit`.

Bun (`https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/` testsuite) and Serde (`serde-rs/serde` `cargo test --workspace`) are covered by `mimalloc-harness projects` / `rust/tests/projects.sh`. Suites must **run** under rewrite, C mimalloc, and libc. Compile/link success is not a substitute. Rewrite-only mismatches vs libc FAIL.

Vulkan Memory Allocator is AMD VMA **3.4** (`libVulkanMemoryAllocator.so.3`). Cover `minAlignment`, dedicated allocate/create (`pMemoryAllocateNext`), and `VmaVulkanFunctions::vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2KHR`. Device tests use fake Vulkan (no GPU). Include a Blender GHOST / OpenXR-style smoke (Vulkan 1.2, buffer device address, mapped sequential-write buffers, GPU-only images, pools, stats/budgets/defrag) in `vma-core` and `mimalloc-harness vma` (`rust/tests/vma-blender.c`). Virtual-block and 3.4 layout smokes stay required.
